      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "heart must certainly be formed of adamantine stone since it",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "has not yet been broken into a hundred pieces.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "34. What is it that lovely-eyed (women) do not do?",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "Having entered the affectionate heart of men they fas-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "cinate them, madden them, mock them, despise them, gladden",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "them and grieve them.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "35. A lion, strong and living on the flesh of elephants",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "and hogs, ruts, it is said, once in a year. The dove eating",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "only hard pebbles ruts daily. Say what the cause here is.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "36 Residence in a sacred forest, and oh joy, association",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "with the deer, sacred maintenance on fruits, stones for couches",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "on the bank of every river—such are the materials for those",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "that like devotion to God. To those whose minds are fixed",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "on renunciation alone, whether (they live in) a house or a",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "forest, it is all the same.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "37. We are quite content with those delicious syllables",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "(utterances) sweeter than honey or clarified butter which the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "Divine speech (the Upanishads) sends forth from its ambro-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "cial and immortal body; as long as there is, under our arm, a",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "quantity of barley-meal procured by begging for our maint-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "enance so long do we not wish to live on wealth acquired by",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "servitude.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r7",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "38. A dog, lean, blind of an eye, lame, crop-eared and",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "tail-less (through disease), suffering from abscesses, clammed",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "with pus, and with his body covered with hundreds of worms,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "exhausted through starvation, decayed with age, and having",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "the brim of an earthen jar placed round its neck, follows a",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "bitch. Madana scruples not to smite even one that has",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "already been smitten.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r8",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "39. Desist, O wise men, from associating with women—",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "from the momentary happiness. Be attached to Mercy,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "Friend-ship and Reason. Neither the fully developed orbs",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "of breasts covered with a wreath, nor the round hips having",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
